        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Walk first, add running in short blocks, and change one thing
            a week.</strong> Twenty to thirty minutes of conversational walking three times a week
            for a fortnight, then incline blocks or one-minute jogs in week three, a little more in
            week four, with any week repeated as often as it needs to be. Add time before pace, and
            let the talk test decide the speed.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Clip the safety key on, keep your hands off the rails after the first minute, slow down
            for five minutes before you step off, and treat lingering joint or tendon pain as a
            signal to go back a week. When the week-four run blocks feel easy, move on to
            <a href="/couch-to-5k-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">couch to 5K on a treadmill</a>.
          </p>
